OL,3,GNEWSARHS says #2.3m M25 works
OL,4,Acompensation 'far short'
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Royal Horticultural Society (RHS)
OL,7,Fhas said compensation for disruption
OL,8,Fcaused by a major road building project
OL,9,Fis "far short" of the amount it lost.
OL,11,FThe #2.3m secured in a settlement from
OL,12,FNational Highways was not sufficient,
OL,13,Fthe RHS said, to compensate for the
OL,14,Fdisruption at its Wisley site, which it
OL,15,Fsays caused #13m losses and led to
OL,16,F350,000 fewer visitors annually.
OL,18,FThe work by National Highways saw
OL,19,Fimprovements on junction 10 of the M25
OL,20,Fand A3, with road closures and
OL,21,Fdiversions between 2022 and 2026.
OL,23,APub: 05-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
